@startuml
title SplitSmart use cases — required product and MVP boundary
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Account holder" as Account
actor "Group member" as Member
actor "Group creator / manager" as Manager
actor "Expense submitter /\npayer" as Submitter
actor "Authorized reviewer\n(policy open)" as Reviewer
actor "Notification recipient" as Recipient

usecase "UC-01 Account lifecycle\n(register/sign in/reset/private data)" as UC1
usecase "UC-02 Manage group and membership" as UC2
usecase "UC-03 Submit expense" as UC3
usecase "UC-04 Review expense" as UC4
usecase "UC-05 View pairwise balances" as UC5
usecase "UC-06 Record payment" as UC6
usecase "UC-07 View expense, balance,\nand payment reports" as UC7
usecase "UC-08 Use supported clients\n(full-product target)" as UC8
usecase "Attach optional receipt" as Receipt
usecase "Choose participants and split" as Split
usecase "Approve expense" as Approve
usecase "Reject expense" as Reject
usecase "View expense notification" as Notification

Account -- UC1
Account -- UC7
Account -- UC8
Member -- UC2
Manager -- UC2
Submitter -- UC3
Reviewer -- UC4
Member -- UC5
Member -- UC6
Recipient -- Notification

UC3 .> Split : <<include>>
Receipt .> UC3 : <<extend>>
Approve .> UC4 : <<extend>>
Reject .> UC4 : <<extend>>
UC3 -- Notification : creates notice

note bottom
Group-manager powers are limited to adding/removing members by the current
requirement. Reviewer eligibility and self-approval are open decisions.
Web, Android, and iOS are required full-product clients (FR-010); this diagram
does not imply they are implemented. The Swing MVP is interim only.
end note
@enduml
